Rule 1 (tensor shapes should be the same)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 3 (first dimension of a tensor matches second dimension of the other)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 1)
>>
Rule 10 (tensor must be at least 2-dimensional)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 11 (tensor must be at least 3-dimensional)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3
>>
Rule 12 (tensor shapes should be the same, but with different dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≠ shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 21 (primitive type variable should not be zero)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≠ 0
>>
Rule 22 (primitive type variable is smaller than the other)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float, v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≤ v_2
